{"id": "sevt_01ByJPt2mU1ywoi3cRU3ctrH", "content": [{"text": "**Checkout deploy `a3f9c21` introduced an N+1 query, which exhausted the DB connection pool and caused the 500s.**\n\n**Timeline**\n- **14:31:18:** `a3f9c21` (\"refactor order summary builder for readability\") deploys to checkout. p99 latency goes from about 75 ms to about 3,800 ms in the same minute.\n- **14:31\u201314:40:** `db_pool_utilization` for checkout climbs steadily, from 0.21 to 0.92.\n- **14:40:** The pool hits 1.0 (50/50 connections, 12 waiters). The first `DB connection pool exhausted` error is logged at 14:40:39. Checkout `error_rate` jumps from 0 to about 0.2\u20130.6 and stays there.\n- **Errors in the log:** There are 70 pool-exhausted errors. The 500s are `PoolTimeout` errors across `/validate` (26), `/summary` (25) and `/submit` (19).\n\n**Mechanism**\n- **Diff:** In `CheckoutSummaryHandler.build_summary`, the old code made one batched `order_id__in` query and grouped the results in memory. The new loop runs one `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` per open order.\n- **Log:** Before the deploy, each request made 1 `db_query` (137 requests). After it, requests average 12.4 and reach up to 16 (268 requests).\n- **Effect:** That is about 12 times the connection hold time per request, so the pool of 50 saturates under normal traffic. Requests then queue and time out.\n\n**Other causes ruled out**\n- **Other deploys:** The cart, auth and inventory deploys don't line up with the checkout change. Cart and auth went out hours earlier, and inventory went out at 14:55, after the errors began.\n- **Other services:** Cart, inventory and auth log no errors after 14:31.\n- **Auth timeouts:** The identity-provider timeouts at 14:15 are in auth and predate the deploy, so they're a separate matter.\n\n**Fix:** Revert `a3f9c21`, or restore the batched query with `order_id__in` and in-memory grouping. The refactor can then be redone without the per-row query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the refactor replaced the single batched `order_items` query with a per-order query in `build_summary`. That N+1 pattern held connections about 12 times longer per request, exhausted the 50-connection checkout DB pool by 14:40, and produced the `PoolTimeout` 500s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T06:00:30.983988Z", "type": "agent.message"}
